{"name":"Big Chill","hex":"#7ecbe2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Big Chill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Synonym of heat death of the universe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Big_Chill"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Big Chill (music festival)","blocks":[{"text":"The Big Chill was an annual festival of alternative, dance and chill-out music and comedy, held in the grounds of Eastnor Castle during early August. The 2011 line-up included The Chemical Brothers, Kanye West, Rodrigo Y Gabriela, Jessie J, Robert Plant, Calvin Harris, Neneh Cherry, Aloe Blacc, Chipmunk, Katy B & Example. The festival has not been staged since 2011."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Big_Chill_2005.jpg/330px-Big_Chill_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Big_Chill_(music_festival)"},{"title":"The Big Chill (film)","blocks":[{"text":"The Big Chill is a 1983 American comedy-drama film directed by Lawrence Kasdan, starring an ensemble cast consisting of Tom Berenger, Glenn Close, Jeff Goldblum, William Hurt, Kevin Kline, Mary Kay Place, Meg Tilly, and JoBeth Williams. The plot focuses on a group of baby boomers who attended the University of Michigan, reuniting after 12 years when their friend Alex commits suicide. It was filmed in Beaufort, South Carolina."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/Big_chill_ver1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Big_Chill_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Tom_Berenger_2019.jpg/500px-Tom_Berenger_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Tom_Berenger_2019.jpg/1280px-Tom_Berenger_2019.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign